# Deepfathom Echo: "At the beginning of combat on your turn, this creature explores. Then you may have it become a copy of another
# creature you control until end of turn." The card revealed is an Island, a land (CR 701.44a): it goes to Bot1's hand and the
# Echo gets no +1/+1 counter. Bot1's only other creature is an Ornithopter, and Bot1 is still asked, because the copy is a "may":
# the Echo is an Ornithopter for the turn (both Ornithopters, no Echo on the battlefield) and a 4/4 Echo again on turn 3, with no
# counter ever put on it (turn 3: it explores another Island and Bot1 chooses none). Bot2's own beginning of combat on turn 4 is not "on your turn": nothing triggers and the library is untouched.

